<!-- Chaos vocations: the four base classes and their ascended classes (docs/CLASSES.md). The Monk, Necromancer and
     Templar lines are in the fragments next to this file (chaos_vocations_monk.xml, chaos_vocations_necro.xml,
     chaos_vocations_templar.xml; their numbers are explained there). server/tools/add_vocations.py installs all of
     them into the base server's data/XML/vocations.xml between "BEGIN chaos vocations" / "END chaos vocations" markers
     (idempotent): an entry of this table replaces the base server's entry with the same id, and the retired ids 2, 6
     and 9 (Druid, Elder Druid, Illusionist) are removed (data/scripts/chaos/class_migration.lua moves their characters
     at the first start: Druid and Illusionist -> Mystic, Elder Druid -> Illusionist).

     | id | class | base | was | client byte |
     |  4 | Warrior      | 4  | Knight            |  1 |
     |  8 | Juggernaut   | 4  | Elite Knight      | 11 |
     | 14 | Berserker    | 4  | (new)             | 21 |
     |  3 | Ranger       | 3  | Paladin           |  2 |
     |  7 | Deadeye      | 3  | Royal Paladin     | 12 |
     | 15 | Beastmaster  | 3  | (new)             | 22 |
     |  1 | Mystic       | 1  | Sorcerer          |  3 |
     |  5 | Elementalist | 1  | Master Sorcerer   | 13 |
     | 10 | Illusionist  | 1  | Arch Illusionist  | 23 |
     | 11 | Thief        | 11 | (phase 1)         |  6 |
     | 12 | Ninja        | 11 | (phase 1)         | 16 |
     | 13 | Samurai      | 11 | (phase 1)         | 26 |
     | 17 | Monk         | 17 | (new, fragment)   |  8 |
     | 18 | Shadowfist   | 17 | (new, fragment)   | 18 |
     | 19 | Iron Sage    | 17 | (new, fragment)   | 28 |
     | 20 | Necromancer  | 20 | (new, fragment)   |  7 |
     | 21 | Lich         | 20 | (new, fragment)   | 17 |
     | 22 | Bone Lord    | 20 | (new, fragment)   | 27 |
     | 23 | Templar      | 23 | (new, fragment)   |  9 |
     | 24 | Inquisitor   | 23 | (new, fragment)   | 19 |
     | 25 | Sentinel     | 23 | (new, fragment)   | 29 |

     Ids that map 1:1 keep their number, so items, spells, NPCs and the database keep working. Both ascended classes of a
     base name it as fromvoc: the engine knows one promotion per vocation, so the choice is made by
     data/scripts/chaos/ascension.lua (!ascend <class>), never by the engine's promotion.

     clientid: the vocation byte of the login packet (0x9F): the base slot (1 warrior, 2 ranger, 3 mystic, 6 thief,
     7 necromancer, 8 monk, 9 templar) + 10 for the first ascended class, + 20 for the second, so the client can
     tell all of them apart (client/base-patches/0016-chaos-vocation-ids.patch maps the bytes back to these ids).

     Gains and skills: Warrior / Juggernaut, Ranger / Deadeye, Mystic / Elementalist are the Knight / Elite Knight, Paladin /
     Royal Paladin and Sorcerer / Master Sorcerer values; the Illusionist keeps the Arch Illusionist's (health 7, mana 27).
     Berserker: the Elite Knight's skills, health 14 / mana 6 per level, weapon hits x1.05, defense and armor x0.9 (it
     trades defence for damage; Rage adds up to +30% as health drops). Beastmaster: the Royal Paladin's skills,
     health 11 / mana 14 / cap 21 per level, distance hits x0.9 (its companion deals the rest).

     The Thief line (phase 1): gains per level between the Knight (cap 25, hp 15, mana 5) and the Paladin (cap 20, hp 10,
     mana 15). attackspeed (ms per weapon swing; every other vocation 2000): with server/src-patches/0002 a weapon's own
     attackspeed is scaled by attackspeed / 2000, so the Thief line stays faster with any weapon. 2026-10-23 (owner: the Thief
     attacks as fast as the Monk): Thief 1500 (was 1600), Ninja 1300 (1400), Samurai 1700 (1800), tied with the Monk line's
     1500 / 1300 / 1700; classes.lua speedComp cuts the weapon hits by the same ratio (Chaos.classes.attackSpeed), so the
     auto attack's damage per second is unchanged. A test keeps the two in step.
     basespeed 230 (others 220). Skills: the three melee skills (sword, club, axe: one melee skill since owner debug item
     46, server/README.md "One melee skill") 1.1 like the Knight's swords, distance 1.2 (shurikens), magic level 2.0 (between the Paladin's 1.4 and the Knight's 3.0).
     formula meleeDamage / distDamage (weapon hits; others 1.0): Thief and Ninja 1.2, Samurai 1.3 (light one-handed blades
     against the Knight's two-handed weapons; measured in server/data/spells/README.md). The Samurai has defense / armor
     1.1, the tankier ascended class. -->
